{"clock":1,"nonce":"66c168af207710ed35102c59e3c24641","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"e2dcf2b3ed83d9ac027fff26227cafd92ab54f89","time":1794171716,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/bimble","event":"issue:6275586519"},"data":{"body":"1. mutualiser les deux premières lignes du bandeau supérieur\n2. ajouter un menu déroulant \"Fichier\" comme pièce jointe\n\u003cimg width=\"549\" height=\"533\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/970477b0-414e-4453-befc-3b75edf1f667\" /\u003e\n3. mettre des icones a la place du texte pour les racourcis \"Save\", \"open\", \"undo\" et \"redo\"\n4. Remplacer l'onglet \"Model\" par \"Project infos\" : dans cet onglet sont rassemblé les outils pour renseigner et connaitre les propriétés et infomations générales du fichier en cours. je veux un bouton \"informations sur le projet\" dans lequel on peut voir et renseigner : numéro du projet, nom du projet, adresse du projet, code postal et ville, numéro de la phase de projet (selon la nomenclature SIA), description de la phase de projet, noms téléphones et adresse postale des intervenants sur le projet. Ces informations sont essentielles car elles seront reprises dans les cartouches des layouts. Je veux aussi un bouton \"paramètres globaux\", un bouton \"Gestion des liens\"\n5. Deuxième onglet : \"Collaborer\". cet onglet sert à gérer les différentes personnes au sein d'un meme bureau qui voudraient travailler sur un meme fichier. Dans cet onglet je veux un bouton \"Gestion des utilisateurs\", qui ouvre un panneau dans lequel on voit la liste des personnes qui travaillent, identifiées par leur adresse mail et un trigrame corespondant a tout ce qu'on trouve dans leur mail avant le \"@\", il faut une colonne qui renseigne leur role sur le projet, puis les autorisations qui en découlent (\"visualisation et sélection seulement\", \"modification\"). Dans cet onglet on gère aussi les calques, équivalent des sous projets dans revit. Il faut un bouton synchroniser pour que les modifications de chaque utilisateur soit ensuite visible chez les autres.\n","title":"modification du bandeau supérieur"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"e2dcf2b3ed83d9ac027fff26227cafd92ab54f89","time":1794230578,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/bimble","event":"issue:6275586519"},"data":{"add":["assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}},{"kind":"comment","author":"61b55b322674a787b89ef011a06fca88d5ce49b7","time":1794221223,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/bimble","event":"comment:6738112355"},"data":{"body":"@cecilemartinier \n1. **Where do we share?** Is a shared folder enough to start (office file server, synced drive)? On a folder, rights are advisory only: anyone who can write to the folder can bypass them. Or do we need a server from day one, so \"view only\" is really enforced?\n2. **Layers = Revit worksets?** Do your current worksets (structure, façade, interior…) map one-to-one onto Bimble layers? Please list the ones you use.\n3. **Borrowed layer: strict or a warning?** When someone has borrowed a layer, should others' edits to it be refused at Synchronize (strict, like Revit), or only flagged with a warning?\n4. **Conflicts:** when two people changed the same field of the same element, is choosing \"keep mine / keep theirs\" per conflict enough, or do you need to see both versions side by side in 3D first?\n5. **Rights:** are \"view and select only\" and \"modify\" the only two rights, or do you need more (e.g. \"modify only my layers\", \"annotate only\")?\n"}},{"kind":"comment","author":"e2dcf2b3ed83d9ac027fff26227cafd92ab54f89","time":1794224989,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/bimble","event":"comment:6739330592"},"data":{"body":"1. We can work just like revit : the “central » model is located on our server here at the office, everyone who has access to the server can access the file and it’s perfectly ok. I know autodesk provide a Cloud service, maybe we will develop that, but later on in the process. The users can change themselves their rights : visualisation or modélisation. Let me explain why I want that : the engineer often does not know the software as well as the drafter, and is afraid he can “break” something when he opens the model. But if he knows his rights to break things are limited it is reassuring for everyone. \n2. Layers = revit workset : pretty much yes, but they should not belong to some particular user. The layers are used to filter the model by other means that the material or the element type. The layer list should be editable. Here is a list to begin with : \n- links\n- levels and grid lines\n- topography\n- excavations\n- Masonry and concrete structure \n- Timber structure\n- timber assembly\n- Steel structure \n- steel assembly\n- MEP"}},{"kind":"comment","author":"e2dcf2b3ed83d9ac027fff26227cafd92ab54f89","time":1794225435,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/bimble","event":"comment:6739464195"},"data":{"body":"3. The layers are not borrowed, only the elements. When a user changes or creates an element, that element belongs to him until he synchronises. After the synchronisation, the other users can change the elements. If you select an object that belongs to another user and want to change it, a pop up warning panel appears saying “this element belongs to user_name” and offering to synchronise or cancel. Then the users need to talk (should we have a chat within the software?). To make it easier we can send a pop up panel to all users that suggest to synchronise twice a day (this is what revit does)"}},{"kind":"comment","author":"e2dcf2b3ed83d9ac027fff26227cafd92ab54f89","time":1794230578,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/bimble","event":"comment:6741128368"},"data":{"body":"5. The different rights are : \"visualisation only\" \" visualisation \u0026 annotation\" \" modelisation \u0026 annotation\". In the future, maybe we'll have one user per project who is \"admin\", and who is the only one who can change other users rights, and by default every new user has the minimum right. But this is a constraint so I'm not 100% sure. For now you can self asign your rights."}}]}